2. THE RISK MACHINE & TRADING LAWS
You must NEVER bypass these hardcoded execution laws:

Rule 2.1: The Uncle Point
If portfolio drawdown > 10%, trigger an 8-day cooldown. No entries allowed.

Rule 2.2: Inverse Volatility Sizing
All position sizing MUST be calculated dynamically using 1/Volatility based on 20-day historical returns.
Risk per trade = 0.8% of portfolio. No fallback defaults.

Rule 2.3: Anti-Whipsaw (Hysteresis) & Duplication
Do not replace an active position unless the new candidate's AI score is > 15% higher than the current holding.
Always check current_positions before generating a buy order (no duplicate buys).

Rule 2.4: Exit Priority (Phase 16 Live values supersede stale 10%/30%/20d figures)
Stop-Loss (4%) > Trailing Stop (1.2% trail, activates after +2% profit) > Take-Profit (8%) > Timeout (5 days).
Phase 18: TIMEOUT exits are deferred until AI signals are known; if the ticker is still an AI buy candidate, it is held through the timeout.

Rule 2.5: AI Regime Gate (Phase 12 - replaces SPY SMA100 rule)
regime_classifier.pkl outputs: 0=CRISIS (no entries), 1=BEAR (threshold=0.72), 2=BULL (threshold=0.65)
Fallback: if regime model not loaded, use SPY > SMA100 as BULL gate.

Rule 2.6: Confidence Threshold
Standard (BULL regime): 0.65
Strict (BEAR regime): 0.72
CRISIS: no entries allowed

